  "id": 461172299,
  "iid": 23772,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "tvbuff: fix Coverity annotations",
  "description": "Coverity annotation name has been changed.\n\nAccording to [C/C++ primitives](https://documentation.blackduck.com/bundle/coverity-docs/page/customizing_coverity/topics/models_primitives/c_models_primitives_c_cpp.html)\n`tainted_data_sanitize` has to been deprecated.\n\n```\n__coverity_tainted_data_sanitize__( void )\nDeprecated: This primitive has been deprecated as of Coverity 2019.09. It is supported for backward compatibility only. Use __coverity_mark_pointee_as_sanitized__() instead.\n```\n\n`__coverity_tainted_data_sanitize__` == `tainted_data_sanitize` annotation\n\n`__coverity_mark_pointee_as_sanitized__` == `taint_sanitize` annotation\n\nTherefore, update in tvbuff is required.\n\nAlso, same annotations need to be added to `tvbuff.h` because of shared functions.\n\n---\n\n**Coverity Annotations in C Files**\n\nCoverity annotations can be added in both C source files (.c) and header files (.h).\n\n- **Code-line Annotations**: These modify the analysis of specific lines of code and can be placed directly in the C source files.\n- **Function Annotations**: These modify the analysis of entire functions and can also be included in header files.\n\nUsing annotations in header files can be beneficial for shared functions or data types across multiple source files, ensuring consistent analysis behavior.\n\n---\n\nI have successfully tested these Coverity annotation changes and those fixed Coverity CID 1680434 in `proto.c`.\n\nCoverity CID 1680434 can be cleared.\n\nAI-assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
